  "builds": "output.s assembled by GNU as (through gcc-14) and linked by GNU ld; and assembled by clang-19 and linked by ld.lld-19. The instructions are not changed; objcopy changes only the symbol table (static entries made global, main renamed).",
  "vectors": "cross product of core values (0, 1, -1, minimum, maximum and others) for up to 4 parameters, a sweep of each parameter over its full value set, and 32 seeded random vectors (64 for wide); loop counts 0 to 8, 16 to 32, 64, 100, 1000 and the maximum",
  "execution": "each call in a forked child with a time limit (20 s; 5 s for a vector without a source result); a brk trap is reported with its immediate",
  "skipped": "a vector for which the source interpreter reports a diagnostic (undefined behavior) or reaches the step limit is not compared with the oracle",
  "upper_bits_probe": "each entry with a 32-bit parameter is also called through a prototype that declares each parameter as a 64-bit integer; the upper 32 bits of each 32-bit argument are DEADBEEF, FFFFFFFF, 00000001 and 80000000 in four calls; each result must be equal to the oracle",
  "static_scan": "control-flow scan of output.s from each entry with a 32-bit parameter: a read of the X form of an argument register before a write to it"
 },
